The fix involves adding a conditional block (`#ifdef CONFIG_LED_FAKE`) to `drivers/led/linux_leds.c`. This block will include `zephyr/drivers/led/led_fake.h`, define the `fake_led_api` using the fake functions, provide a simple `fake_led_init` function, and finally use `DEVICE_DT_DEFINE(DT_NODELABEL(fake_leds), ...)` to instantiate the `fake_leds` device.

This ensures that when `CONFIG_LED_FAKE` is enabled (as it is for the test), the `fake_leds` device object is properly defined and linked, resolving the `undefined reference` error.

